  "body": "Closes #1310\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (w1310)\n\n### Problem\nLegacy plays a light impact in four places SwiftHFR stays silent: the Favoris empty state's « Afficher les sections repliées » and « Tout déplier » (`Favorites.swift:623-629`), search results arriving (`ForumSearchView.swift:92`), and the reader's refresh at start and at completion (`MessagesView.swift:5051-5053`, `:5153-5157`), all @ 87fe0d1c. The profile haptic belongs to the unported smiley toggle: out of scope.\n\n### Change\n- `FavoritesOptionsModel`: `showCollapsedSectionsFromEmptyState()` and `expandAllFromEmptyState()` play one light impact; the empty state's two buttons call them. The menu toggles stay silent, as in legacy.\n- `ForumSearchModel`: one light impact when a search or a results page is applied (empty answer included; failure, refused query, superseded load: none), as legacy's success branch.\n- `ReaderRefresh.run` (the shared path of the button and the pull): one impact before the request and one after it, loaded or failed, as legacy's `finishRefreshHapticIfNeeded` (called on failure too). A refresh the model refuses (composer open) is silent. The pull keeps its own start impact (`startsWithHaptic: false`), so it plays two in all, never three.\n- All through `HapticFeedback` (injected, default `.live`), so « Retours haptiques » governs them. No `.sensoryFeedback`. GAP-149 already reads \"same toggle\": no ledger entry.\n- GAP-1207 (the pull) gets a `gap-edit` in the Ledger below: the pull plays a start and a completion impact. GAP-149 itself is unchanged.\n- Does not touch RootModel or tab code (#1318).\n\n### Tests\n`LegacyHapticsTests` (13 tests, incl. refresh refused under an open composer: no haptic, no request; empty search answer: one impact; recorder injected as in `HapticFeedbackTests`): each haptic once, order relative to the request, silence with the setting off, silence on failure / refused query / menu toggles; `ReaderBottomBarTests` pull test now expects the completion impact too.\nRun on iPhone 18 Pro iOS 27.2, unsigned: green (75 tests, 6 suites: LegacyHapticsTests, ReaderBottomBarTests, ForumSearchModelTests, FavoritesOptionsModelTests, FavoritesListModelTests, HapticFeedbackTests).\nRed by mutation (haptic calls removed from the Favoris methods, the search `if arrived`, the reader completion impact): 9 issues, 7 in LegacyHapticsTests and 2 in the pull test (`Expectation failed: recorder.played == [light]`, `seenAtPlay == [0, 1]`, etc.).\n\n### SwiftLint by hand\nline_length (no line over 140), file_length, type_body_length (test helpers moved to an extension), trailing closure labels (one closure per call), no new branches in functions beyond one `if` each.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-1207\nSwiftHFR final: Pull past the top or the end of the page: an icon grows with the pull, one haptic and the refresh come when it is full, once per touch, the reading position is kept, and a second light impact plays when the refresh completes, loaded or failed (#1310); no end-of-page hint (#1207, #820).\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
