   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 1, reviewer r1321 (Opus 5.5), author w1310 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1321, head 2ea3374d)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\nEvery trigger matches legacy at 87fe0d1c:\n- Favoris: both empty-state buttons play, and the menu toggles stay silent (`Favorites.swift:623-629`).\n- Search: on every successful load, page changes and empty answers included; never on a failure, an empty query or a superseded load (`ForumSearchView.swift:76-92`).\n- Reader « Actualiser »: once at the start and once at completion, failure included (`MessagesView.swift:3793, 5051-5053, 5152-5156`).\n- Pull: two impacts in all, as legacy; the `ReaderBottomBarTests:299` expectation is correct.\n\nNo overlap with #1318. `ReaderRefresh.run` keeps its order.\n\n1. **Low**, `ReaderPageEnd.swift:85-91`. The claim that a refresh refused while a composer is open stays silent has no test: removing the `!refuses` guards leaves every test green. Fix: open a composer (`model.composer(.reply, isOpen: true)`, as `ReaderComposerSuspensionTests:28` does), `run`, and expect no haptic and no request.\n2. **Low**, GAP-1207 (`GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:108`). It says the pull plays one haptic, but after this PR the pull plays a second one at completion. Fix: a `### Ledger` `gap-edit` on GAP-1207's SwiftHFR column (start and completion impacts, #1310).\n3. **Nit**, `LegacyHapticsTests.swift:208`. \"Empty answer included\" has no test: add an empty `searchPage` case.\n4. **Nit (information)**, `ReaderPageEnd.swift:91`. When a newer load supersedes a refresh, the completion impact plays when the refresh returns, while legacy plays it when the newer load lands. Same count.\n\nChecked by reading: no line over 140, files under 400 lines, type bodies under 250 (241 for `ReaderBottomBarTests`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
